;; Inference on the device: a runtime, a model, and a service that runs one
;; against the other.
;;
;; The model is the interesting part. It is a file with a version, a licence,
;; a training provenance and an input shape, and none of that is anything
;; Kconfig knows about. What Silt can do is carry it, check it exists before
;; anything builds, and put its contents in the solution hash — so "which
;; model shipped on which device" has an answer that is not a spreadsheet.
;;
;; What Silt cannot do, and this pack does not pretend to: say the model is
;; accurate, that its operators are supported by the runtime, or that the
;; numbers match a workstation. Those are the customer's problem. They are
;; easier to solve on a base that can be explained.

(pack inference
  (version "0.1.0")
  (doc "TensorFlow Lite and a carried model, run as a service")

  (requires
    (buildroot "2025.02.16"))

  (external "br2-external")

  (provides
    (feature inference)))
